# TODO - The Simpsons: Hit & Run

## Objective

PC, selected base preference. Reconstruct the driving, missions and open world
independently.

## Acceptance

- Study the maintainer's local remaster under
  `.reference/games/simpsons-hit-and-run/src/` and its accompanying
  documentation before designing the 3D implementation. Identify reusable
  mechanisms, including cameras, animation, vehicle physics, world
  streaming, rendering and spatial audio; extend the shared Rust engine,
  platform IR and importer rather than creating a title-specific engine.
- Review component provenance and licence compatibility before using any
  code. Use only lawfully available reference material; independently
  implement observable behaviour where reuse is not authorized. Do not
  ship the reference source, documentation or original media.
- Admit only files verified as part of the selected original PC edition.
  The required runtime data must be reconstructible from original retail
  RCF archives, RMV movies and other verified retail data. Inspect full
  container indexes before defining mandatory loose files. Resolve P3D
  assets and other resources from admitted containers when present.
  Require a loose P3D only when it is necessary, absent from the admitted
  containers and verified as independently distributed retail data.
  Never require an extracted duplicate or infer retail provenance from
  a filename or extension alone.
- Treat maintainer-added art, extracted scripts, converted movies, design
  documents and other derived material as optional research only. Never
  require the remaster source, extra assets, modified executables, no-CD
  variants, common-byte artifacts or proprietary runtime DLLs to import,
  build or play the independent reconstruction.
- Implement original-format admission and conversion through the shared
  importer IR. Verify a minimal retail-only fixture, with optional
  reference materials absent. Test equivalent container-backed and loose
  retail resource admission without requiring duplicate external files.
  Reject missing required data and malformed
  containers; never silently substitute maintainer-added content.
- Preserve the single configured canonical asset store and use bounded,
  preferably in-memory tests. Do not duplicate the retail input set.

- Use only a selected lawful original edition and locally imported assets.
- Reuse shared engine mechanisms and extend them where necessary.
- Verify observable gameplay or application behaviour, saves and input.
- Report actual Linux, Android and browser acceptance where applicable.
- Run `cargo validate` and record unresolved parity or platform limits.

- Check original input under
  `.reference/games/simpsons-hit-and-run/`.
- If required media is missing, record the blocker in Evidence; recheck
  and clear it when a suitable original edition becomes available.

## Evidence

Local input is present; original-edition admission and playable parity are
not yet verified. A read-only inspection on 2026-11-25 found 13 RCF files,
17 RMV files and 1,965 P3D files in the mixed local assets directory.
Sample headers were consistent with Radcore Cement Library, Bink and P3D
containers. Bounded inspection of the first 256 KiB of each RCF showed
audio resource paths and audio scripts in scripts.rcf. It did not
establish full container contents or the necessity of loose P3D files.
The local assets README explicitly identifies executable
comparison artifacts and no-CD variants; they are not required inputs.
The maintainer confirms that other extra materials are also present.

The local remaster contains 2,055 C++ source/header files, including
distinct renderer, simulation, camera, loading, mission and sound
subsystems. Its shader migration notes describe OpenGL 3.3+ skinning
and CPU fallback. Reference study is required, but provenance, build
status, the exact minimal original file set and import support remain
unverified. Keep this task open.
